---
description: Project-wide conventions
globs: "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read `AGENTS.md` at repo root before making non-trivial changes — it has the architecture, stack, requirement IDs (R1-R9), and current status.
- This is a two-service monorepo (`apps/web`, `apps/worker`) sharing `packages/shared-types`. Don't duplicate type definitions across services — put shared shapes in `packages/shared-types`.
- Scope out of bounds unless explicitly asked: mobile/PWA, production DevOps hardening, large-scale storage optimisation, AI audio tagging.
- When a change implements or touches a requirement (R1-R9), mention the requirement ID in the PR/commit description.
- Prefer small, single-purpose commits/PRs over large multi-feature ones — this is a 4-person team project with PR review required before merge to `main`.
- No fixed roles — everyone works across web, worker, and DB schema. After finishing a feature, update `PROGRESS.md` (what shipped, what's next, new decisions) so later sessions have continuity. If the work creates, changes, or closes a risk, update `RISK_REGISTER.md` in the same PR.
- For a repeatable multi-step workflow (e.g. adding a new feature end-to-end), check `.cursor/skills/` first instead of improvising each time.
